{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_019gf8HaohUU6RGnXXsFELjh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q2: How would you design an LLM-powered enterprise search system?**\n\nThe note covers the four distinguishing design planes that separate a production enterprise search platform from a basic RAG demo:\n\n1. **Connectors & Ingestion** — source-specific adapters (Confluence, Slack, GitHub, Salesforce, SharePoint) normalizing into a canonical schema with checksums for change detection\n2. **ACL-Aware Index** — the hardest and most critical piece: every chunk carries its authorized user/group list as metadata; ACL filtering enforced at the vector-DB layer (Pinecone/Qdrant metadata filter), not just in application code\n3. **Retrieval & Ranking** — query intent classification (navigation → skip LLM; factual → synthesis; exploratory → multi-chunk synthesis) + hybrid HNSW+BM25 with RRF + cross-encoder reranking\n4. **Quality Loop** — golden query set, RAGAS offline metrics, production CTR/thumbs/zero-result-rate signals, and implicit reranker fine-tuning from clicked results\n\nKey pitfalls covered: skipping ACL enforcement, using one embedding model for all source types, calling GPT-4 on every query regardless of complexity, and having no plan for freshness on real-time sources like Slack."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":62304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":374,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecde46b0-4350-4d47-bea0-25f0d76195f5","uuid":"690e9885-36cb-4042-9c32-787bb469b82c"}
